  "body": "The following inputs in `<!--<!--!>` and `<!--<!--!` from whatwg/html/pull/1356 give following results when parsed using [parsetree](https://checker.html5.org/parsetree/) `<!--!>` and `<!--!` (with parse errors which I'll ignore). \r\n\r\nHowever, following [html spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/) I wasn't able to manually reconstruct how that result achieved. My state machine and hand verification return following states for `<!--<!--!>`\r\n\r\n```\r\nData state + `<` => \r\nTag Open state + `!` =>\r\nMarkup Declaration state + `--` =>\r\nComment start state + `<` =>\r\nComment + ``<`` =>                                   |    CommentToken (\"<\")\r\nComment less than sign state + `!`     =>            |    CommentToken (\"<!\")\r\nComment less than sign bang state + `-`  =>          |    CommentToken (\"<!\")\r\nComment less than sign bang dash state + `-` =>      |    CommentToken (\"<!\")\r\nComment less than sign bang dash dash state + `!` => |    CommentToken (\"<!\") + Error\r\nComment end state ``!`` =>                           |    CommentToken (\"<!\") + Error\r\nComment end bang state `>` =>                        |    CommentToken (\"<!\") + Error\r\n\r\nEmit comment \"<!\" and two Errors\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs there error in spec, parse tree or my transcription of the new comments rule?\r\n    ",
